	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg10145"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=393" title="View the profile of Zerxes">Zerxes</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 51<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=393"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10145#msg10145"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10145#msg10145">Re: Future of EQ</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #10 on:</b> August 17, 2004, 12:42:53 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Well, he (Delheru) is right that the encounters will only be challenging until the strategy is worked out.&nbsp; But as far as organization goes, is this not the same as mob strategy?&nbsp; Will it be challenging only until you have the &quot;organization strategy&quot; (timing buffing so everyone is ready to fight quickly as soon as people are FM before the buffs wear off, etc.) figured out for any given encounter?&nbsp; I mean, if we clear to the set up spot, clear the adds leading to the boss, raid leader calls out &quot;BUFF NOW!&quot;, and the buffing classes have already pre-arranged how that is going to work, they buff, raid leader calls out &quot;MOVE&quot;, and you fight the target - its not rocket science and people will get this &quot;strategy&quot; aspect down just as they do the actual mob strategy.&nbsp; Perhaps an oversimplification, but I think you understand my point.&nbsp; As far as hours of recovery in the event of a wipe, I just don&#039;t see how that adds to the challenge of the game - its just the punishment for failing (which again, some may view as a good thing).<br /><br />As for EQ&#039;s future, I don&#039;t see Sony pulling the plug on it due to people not playing it any time soon, but I think there definitely is a trend of many of the game&#039;s senior players leaving for what they view as greener pastures (WoW and EQ2).&nbsp; Blizzard has been pretty damm smart in extending &quot;guild beta invitations&quot; - as was said above, &quot;friends&quot; are what keep people returning to EQ.&nbsp; If you get the group of friends to leave EQ, problem solved.<br /><br />As far as EQ2 being more &quot;casual&quot; friendly, I&#039;m not too sure about that - I know that the game&#039;s encounters are designed for groups of up to 24 people, but I&#039;m not sure that necessarily means the game itself is &quot;casual.&quot;&nbsp; I think one lesson that developers have learned (or better have learned by now) is that too much catering to the &quot;casual&quot; player = kiss of death for a MMORPG.&nbsp; If the game&#039;s rewards are too easily obtainable, it won&#039;t take long for players to grow bored of the game and they quit.&nbsp; You HAVE to keep that carrot dangling in front of players to keep them logging in and playing.&nbsp; They HAVE to some reason to keep playing.<br /><br />P.S.&nbsp; Callon - I play on average 15 or so hours a week and do just fine in EQ1&nbsp; <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/wiggle2.gif" alt="Wiggle" border="0" /><br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg10153"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=426" title="View the profile of Transhade">Transhade</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 15<br />
