	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg10195"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=570" title="View the profile of Castamist">Castamist</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 32<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								<a href="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/about_me/1,,,00.html?Uin=4859621" target="_blank"><img src="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/online?icq=4859621&amp;img=5" alt="4859621" width="18" height="18" border="0" /></a>
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=570"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:castamist@hotmail.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10195#msg10195"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10195#msg10195">Re: Future of EQ</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #12 on:</b> August 18, 2004, 12:25:16 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Hmmm.. My thoughts....<br /><br />I think that Everquest has been and will continue to slow down but I don&#039;t think a new and improved game will be the culprit, merely a contributing factor.<br /><br />Everquest was completely player-to-player dependant when I first started.  If  ports were needed, you&#039;d have to talk to somebody.  Grouping was necessary and required a slower or healer, a tank..etc. You <span style="text-decoration: underline;">HAD</span> to communicate with each other and work together. <br /><br />Now days, most people don&#039;t need a lot of player-to-player communication because a lot are self-sufficient. Boxing one, two, or three+ accounts of alts and twinks they don&#039;t need anyone else.  The nexus spires or PoK-books to travel and many people sell their buffs in PoK.  The bazaar allows you to get what you need, day or night, without having to talk to anyone.  I lost count on how many people I know that box clerics.<br /><br />Anyways, that&#039;s my thoughts. I won’t be spending a lot of time and energy in another game and with server lockdowns and patches to fix patches that EQ has now plus additional hardware requirements, I know I won’t be going EQ2.<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Castamist - 65 Archon - RN
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg10197"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174" title="View the profile of Delheru">Delheru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 104<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10197#msg10197"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10197#msg10197">Re: Future of EQ</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #13 on:</b> August 18, 2004, 12:43:38 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10145#msg10145">Quote from: Zerxes on August 17, 2004, 12:42:53 pm</a></div><div class="quote">Well, he (Delheru) is right that the encounters will only be challenging until the strategy is worked out.  But as far as organization goes, is this not the same as mob strategy?</div><br />Not at all actually.Ascent was superbly organized quite regardless of whether we knew a tactic or not. This resulted in:<br />- FAST corpse recoveries  (this was actually hard way back when, now it&#039;s a joke)<br />- FAST rebuffs<br />- loot distribution which never slowed our advancement (whereas DA/EiE still spent 1h30min doing loot on PoTime clears, whereas it didn&#039;t affect our clear times at all)<br />- extremely fast gathering in race situations (showed this off at Fennin many times... lots done in earlier expansions as well)<br />etc etc<br />- Fast group forming and optimization (seldom have to wait long for groups etc)<br />- Communicating well, with everyone getting the information they need.<br />- Keeping the force happy and focused/assisting etc<br /><br />These are totally mob independent abilities. <br />First one got trivialized by res sticks, GYs etc. <br />Second one trivialized by first group buffs, then target group buff, then mgb.<br />Third one is the only one totally untouched by SOE. I&#039;m just waiting for them to introduce an inbuilt dkp system.<br />Fourth one is pointless with instancing. Not to mention PoK makes going from here to there totally trivial (used to need ports).<br />Fifth one has been made easier by /raid, though still requires significant work. (though I hear now raidleader can swap people around groups, so it&#039;s getting easier)<br />Sixth one was trivialized to a great part by the channel system.<br />Seventh one was helped a lot by /raid  (not sharing exp used to get a lot of grumbling on VT clears)<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"> its not rocket science and people will get this &quot;strategy&quot; aspect down just as they do the actual mob strategy.</div><br />Dunno about that. If it was that simple, the server must be fielding an average IQ of like 70, since we were the only guild to do well in all of those fields, and even we were significantly lacking at times (our loot distribution was at times rather inefficient... as in the loot rotting that would have been upgrades etc). However a great many guilds figured out strategies for about a billion mobs between a_small_rat00 and, say, Rallos_Zek00. Can you point out a single guild that is &#039;flawless&#039; in the organizational issues I mentioned?  (before the trivializations anyway)<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">As far as hours of recovery in the event of a wipe, I just don&#039;t see how that adds to the challenge of the game - its just the punishment for failing (which again, some may view as a good thing).</div><br />If it takes the &#039;next man&#039; 10min to recover and you 1h to recover, is this still &quot;punishment for failing&quot;? I&#039;d call it punishment for sucking.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg10211"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=773" title="View the profile of Cocomo">Cocomo</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 14<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/terminator.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Retired Paladin<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=773"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10211#msg10211"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10211#msg10211">Re: Future of EQ</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #14 on:</b> August 18, 2004, 09:07:13 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I think EQ is already seeing the beginning of its end days.&nbsp; In fact, when I thought again, EQ has been pretty much dead since release of Velious; we just didn&#039;t recognize it.&nbsp; The reason: lack of innovation.&nbsp; Original Everquest was innovative, and new; it forces you to level up so that you can explore, and to explore more so that you can level up.&nbsp; Then Kunark came, pretty much of a time sink -- you can pretty much grind in 2-3 zones and level up; no real meaning of faction alignments.&nbsp; Then Velious came, and put sense of exploration back into the game.&nbsp; The graphics got better, and there was some real meaning to faction alignment, although Velious factions (except Tunare) were not much related to the old world faction.&nbsp; Raid wise, it was also the most fun and competitive thing.&nbsp; There&#039;s natural path of progression, and natural time sinks -- like gearing up, first with Thurgadin gear, then Skyshrine or Kael, then you could really raid North ToV or ST.&nbsp; By natural time sink, I mean some deterrance to your progression which one must overcome, but one has fun working on it.<br /><br />To me that was the expansion that I had most fun with.&nbsp; Luclin graphics were good but what did they add to actual game play experience?&nbsp; Both Luclin and PoP were pretty much like Kunark -- artificial time sinks and no real meaning of faction alignment.<br /><br />Everquest is fun not because of its graphics, or its (buggy) quests, or its not so intelligent AI engine behind mobs, or even its lore and game play.&nbsp; Everquest is fun, and addicting, because of players like you.&nbsp; We learned to depend on each other, got attached to each other, while trying to achieve our common goal; i.e., to excape our daily lives from realities of so called real life and live in this fantasy world, a few hours a day.&nbsp; Of course, along came grinds, raids, corpse runs, weddings, romance, drama, trains, competition, looking for groups, selling/buying goods, kill stealing, ninja looting, and so on.&nbsp; Scary, fantasy now imitates reality!&nbsp; Some power gamers from some uber guilds may not agree with it, but it is the reason that the rest of us play -- to escape from daily lives.<br /><br />I can tell you this.&nbsp; There are quite a few new games on the horizon to replace Everquest -- WoW, EQ2, Vanguard (by original EQ creators), just to name a few.&nbsp; But for the new game to be as popular and as addicting as Everquest, it must provide a meaningful way that players interact with and depend on each other.<br /><br />Just like you, I can&#039;t wait to find out what that game would be.<br /><br />See you in the next game!<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
<a name="lastPost"></a>
